interpretation:
The walkthrough turns the completed deterministic Full WOW v1.2 product trace into a human-readable terminal story.

It shows:
- business modules observed the supplier payment / shipment review scene;
- DRS remembered prior traces but did not decide;
- AVF hard-masked unsafe routes and ranked safe directions without authorizing;
- Root created one scoped Supplier A ActionCommitPacket model;
- MockBankSandbox consumed only that scoped packet;
- the corridor validated scope, adapter, expiry, idempotency, amount, creditor, payment slot, and forbidden surfaces;
- the corridor created mock payment intent, consent, and order;
- the corridor returned mock receipt evidence;
- receipt is evidence only;
- Supplier B remained blocked;
- shipment remained held;
- no real payment, real bank call, shipment release, or real-world effect happened;
- Root remained final authority.

